WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:11.760
I was either stranded in here, ALONE, with this likely predator...

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:15.120
Or stranded out there in the middle of a lockdown...

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:23.440
Hello, and welcome to Al Dente Creepypasta,
horror stories cooked to perfection with a

00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:30.930
splash of red sauce My name is CZ and I will
be your server this episode.

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:35.609
Morning classes with horrible teachers are
hard enough to get through without an insane

00:00:35.609 --> 00:00:38.829
clown on the loose in the school.

00:00:38.829 --> 00:00:43.750
Today’s story takes us through the worst
day of school.

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:45.510
Let’s dig right in.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.080
“I heard he has a thing going on with that
girl...

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:52.880
Gina Wendelvon!” she half-whispered.

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:59.200
We were sitting in the back of 2nd period
science as my best friend Lexi spilled the

00:00:59.219 --> 00:01:04.330
tea on the latest rumors about Mr. Markham,
the history teacher slash volleyball coach

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:08.040
who’s been the subject of some pretty messed
up rumors as of late.

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:12.010
Lexi: “Leslie Franklin was supposedly upstairs
getting something from her locker after practice

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:17.170
one night, and saw Gina coming out from a
“private tutoring session” with Mr. Markham!”

00:01:17.170 --> 00:01:18.170
“Eww!

00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:20.410
Why the hell would Gina even want to?”

00:01:20.410 --> 00:01:25.100
Lexi: “She must REALLY need an A in US History.”

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:26.620
“That’s so gross!

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:28.650
Eww, eww, eww, no!

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:30.640
He’s old.”

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:33.730
Lexi: “From what I heard, she wouldn’t
be the first.”

00:01:33.730 --> 00:01:38.330
What she was telling me was, sadly, probably
true.

00:01:38.330 --> 00:01:43.400
The rumors about Mr. Markham had swirled into
a frenzy since the winter break incident,

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:48.750
when he had supposedly given Kim Ichikawa
a ride home after the last Volleyball practice

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:51.200
while her parents were gone.

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:54.160
The bell rang.

00:01:54.160 --> 00:01:56.710
“Do you think it’s true though?”

00:01:56.710 --> 00:02:01.860
Lexi asked me, as I dropped off my science
textbook in my locker, exchanging it for my

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:02.860
US History book.

00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:06.800
“I don’t know, why don’t you ask him?”

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:08.560
I told her mockingly.

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:11.300
We both had Mr. Markham next period together.

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:13.750
“I bet you could find out Evanna.

00:02:13.750 --> 00:02:15.859
I think he likes you!”

00:02:15.859 --> 00:02:16.879
“Eww…

00:02:16.879 --> 00:02:17.900
No…

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:19.770
And once again: Eww!”

00:02:19.770 --> 00:02:22.049
“He does call on you a lot.

00:02:22.049 --> 00:02:24.190
Like a lot a lot.”

00:02:24.190 --> 00:02:26.170
“Nope . Don’t care.”

00:02:26.170 --> 00:02:28.140
Evanna: “Darn it!

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:29.459
Not again!”

00:02:29.459 --> 00:02:32.930
The locker had snagged a bit of the skirt
I was wearing and it was pinched inside my

00:02:32.930 --> 00:02:33.930
locker door.

00:02:33.930 --> 00:02:38.480
Lexi: “Come on, we’re gonna be late!”

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:42.109
“You could be like a school hero.

00:02:42.109 --> 00:02:45.000
Expose him for what he really is and get him
fired!”

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:50.080
We were sitting IN Mr. Markham’s class now,
and I didn’t want to have this discussion

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:52.700
with him in the room.

00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:54.209
She was right though.

00:02:54.209 --> 00:02:59.140
Of the four students that he had “randomly”
called on this lesson, three of them were

00:02:59.140 --> 00:03:00.140
me.

00:03:00.140 --> 00:03:02.700
“Lexi, can we please have this discussion
some other--”

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:03.700
Mr Markham: “Evanna!

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:06.519
You’re not talking during my lecture now
are you?”

00:03:06.519 --> 00:03:08.739
My heart skipped a beat.

00:03:08.739 --> 00:03:10.909
Had he overheard us talking about him?

00:03:10.909 --> 00:03:14.569
Mr Markham: “If you have something to say
about District of Columbia v. Heller, why

00:03:14.569 --> 00:03:16.519
don’t you share it with the class?”

00:03:16.519 --> 00:03:19.519
“No, I don’t sir.”

00:03:19.519 --> 00:03:23.430
He paused and stared at me for a moment before
continuing his lesson.

00:03:23.430 --> 00:03:24.430
Really?

00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:27.499
In front of the whole class?

00:03:27.499 --> 00:03:29.370
He must really be getting cocky.

00:03:29.370 --> 00:03:31.090
“Thanks a lot…”

00:03:31.090 --> 00:03:32.639
I muttered to Lexi.

00:03:32.639 --> 00:03:34.189
Mr Markham: “Evanna!

00:03:34.189 --> 00:03:35.540
See me after the bell!”

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:39.670
The whole class ‘ooed’ at this, and I
rolled my eyes.

00:03:39.670 --> 00:03:40.670
Great.

00:03:40.670 --> 00:03:48.060
The last thing I wanted was to be one-on-one
with the biggest creep teacher in the school.

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:52.340
When class let out, Lexi told me she’d wait
out for me in the hall.

00:03:52.340 --> 00:03:57.779
Mr. Markham waited for the whole class to
empty out, then closed the door.

00:03:57.779 --> 00:04:00.209
I remained at my desk.

00:04:00.209 --> 00:04:03.419
He didn’t say anything at first.

00:04:03.419 --> 00:04:09.469
He took his time walking over and sitting
on the desk directly in front of me.

00:04:09.469 --> 00:04:14.260
He stared at me for a moment, then sighed,
as if he were still contemplating whether

00:04:14.260 --> 00:04:16.470
or not he was going to punish me.

00:04:16.470 --> 00:04:22.049
The silence was uncomfortable.

00:04:22.049 --> 00:04:26.790
Then he went into this rant, about how he
was supposedly concerned with my performance

00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:30.190
lately, how it was reflected by behaviour
in class.

00:04:30.190 --> 00:04:31.450
It was all bull.

00:04:31.450 --> 00:04:34.690
He wouldn’t shut up though.

00:04:34.690 --> 00:04:37.500
He was going to make me late for my next class
at this point.

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:39.540
I saw Lexi waiting outside the door.

00:04:39.540 --> 00:04:43.490
I wanted to signal her to just go on without
me, but her back was turned.

00:04:43.490 --> 00:04:46.380
Mr Markham: “This is exactly the kind of
thing I’m talking about!

00:04:46.380 --> 00:04:48.280
Are you even paying attention?”

00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:49.780
“I just…”

00:04:49.780 --> 00:04:50.900
He interrupted me.

00:04:50.900 --> 00:04:53.370
He started asking me all these questions.

00:04:53.370 --> 00:04:55.260
Is there something going on with my life?

00:04:55.260 --> 00:04:59.200
Is there something wrong at home?

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:04.010
The passing period ended, but he told me he’d
write me a pass to my next class.

00:05:04.010 --> 00:05:08.100
Then things started getting really weird.

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:11.850
He started asking personal questions.

00:05:11.850 --> 00:05:13.810
If there’s something else distracting me.

00:05:13.810 --> 00:05:15.970
If I had a boyfriend.

00:05:15.970 --> 00:05:18.110
I needed to get out of here.

00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:21.970
I made up some story about being overwhelmed
by my school work.

00:05:21.970 --> 00:05:26.470
I don’t know why I thought that would get
him to let me go, but I think it had the opposite

00:05:26.470 --> 00:05:31.660
effect, so I froze for a moment, then stood
up out of my chair.

00:05:31.660 --> 00:05:35.710
He gets to his feet as well, with a scary
look in his eyes.

00:05:35.710 --> 00:05:39.520
Before it could escalate any further, an announcement
comes over the intercom.

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:43.500
“Attention!

00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:44.160
Attention!

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:46.580
All classes are hereby suspended into lockdown.

00:05:46.580 --> 00:05:48.970
ALL classes are hereby suspended into lockdown!”

00:05:48.970 --> 00:05:56.690
It took probably about 15 seconds for the
reality of the situation to sink in…

00:05:56.690 --> 00:06:04.470
I was either stranded in here, alone... with
this likely predator… or stranded out there,

00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:09.640
alone… in the middle of a lockdown.

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:19.960
Mr. Markham told me to get against the wall
near the door as he turned off the lights.

00:06:20.840 --> 00:06:25.000
He came and sat RIGHT next to me on the floor.

00:06:25.010 --> 00:06:26.810
Uncomfortably so.

00:06:26.810 --> 00:06:28.880
My head was spinning out of control.

00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:33.110
That’s when I realized… the door!

00:06:33.110 --> 00:06:34.940
Nobody had locked the door!

00:06:34.940 --> 00:06:41.910
I looked to the door and realized, there was
someone standing RIGHT on the other side of

00:06:41.910 --> 00:06:43.130
it.

00:06:43.130 --> 00:06:50.530
Not daring to budge or make a sound, I tried
to conceal my breathing, taking slow deep

00:06:50.530 --> 00:06:51.920
breaths.

00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:02.760
The footsteps stopped in front of the door.

00:07:02.760 --> 00:07:04.590
I was shaking.

00:07:04.600 --> 00:07:07.380
But the room was quiet.

00:07:09.920 --> 00:07:11.480
*door handle sound*

00:07:11.600 --> 00:07:14.680
Whoever was standing out there, had tried
to get in.

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:18.770
The door was ALREADY locked.

00:07:18.770 --> 00:07:24.050
I didn’t know if I should be relieved to
safe or outraged that Mr. Markham had LOCKED

00:07:24.050 --> 00:07:27.740
ME IN to our conversation after class.

00:07:27.740 --> 00:07:31.220
The intruder continued to stand outside the
door.

00:07:31.220 --> 00:07:33.860
Then suddenly…

00:07:33.860 --> 00:07:35.180
*SMASH*

00:07:35.180 --> 00:07:39.730
The entire room seemed to shake as the guy
threw his body against the door!

00:07:39.730 --> 00:07:43.980
He tried this a second time before the sound
of a girl screaming could be heard from down

00:07:43.980 --> 00:07:45.050
the hall.

00:07:45.050 --> 00:07:50.390
What happened next took the horrors I had
experienced up to that point, and twisted

00:07:50.390 --> 00:07:55.000
them into something ten times more terrifying.

00:07:55.000 --> 00:08:04.780
The guy on the other side of the door, started
blowing this clown horn, over and over.

00:08:04.780 --> 00:08:09.220
The sound drifted away from our door and toward
the screaming girl who continued to shriek

00:08:09.220 --> 00:08:10.900
and call for help.

00:08:10.900 --> 00:08:14.120
*screams, clown horn*

00:08:14.120 --> 00:08:17.980
I looked to Mr. Markham as if to suggest he
should go out there and try to help this girl.

00:08:17.980 --> 00:08:20.050
He avoided my eye contact.

00:08:20.050 --> 00:08:22.360
Freaking coward!

00:08:23.120 --> 00:08:24.480
*big bang*

00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:32.560
All at once, the screaming and the clown horn
stopped at the sound of a thud.

00:08:32.570 --> 00:08:37.430
I gasped, because the severity of the situation
had hit me.

00:08:37.430 --> 00:08:41.890
This wasn’t just another drill, this is
the real thing.

00:08:41.890 --> 00:08:48.800
What schools all across the country practice
lockdowns for… was this...

00:08:48.800 --> 00:08:54.460
This person, this intruder with the clown
horn wasn’t just pulling some kind of joke…

00:08:54.460 --> 00:08:57.690
he was dangerous.

00:08:57.690 --> 00:09:02.680
My mind went to a dark place: a worst possible
scenario.

00:09:02.680 --> 00:09:04.360
And it hit me hard.

00:09:04.360 --> 00:09:07.130
My eyes started to blur with tears.

00:09:07.130 --> 00:09:12.580
I buried my head in my hands, just trying
to focus on taking deep breaths.

00:09:12.580 --> 00:09:19.890
THEN I FELT A COLD PAIR OF HANDS ON MY SHOULDERS.

00:09:19.890 --> 00:09:23.360
...and they started to caress me.

00:09:23.360 --> 00:09:27.400
That mother****ing pig.

00:09:27.400 --> 00:09:31.650
He was using this HORRIBLE situation to his
advantage.

00:09:31.650 --> 00:09:37.540
He was trying to take advantage of me at my
most vulnerable moment.

00:09:37.540 --> 00:09:42.360
And maybe the worst part was that I was trapped.

00:09:42.360 --> 00:09:47.330
I couldn’t make even a sound without putting
my own life in danger.

00:09:47.330 --> 00:09:50.840
At this point, I didn’t care anymore.

00:09:50.840 --> 00:09:54.890
I didn’t care about the lockdown, the intruder,
any of it.

00:09:54.890 --> 00:09:57.920
I needed to get out of this room... now!

00:09:57.920 --> 00:10:03.050
I pulled away from his grip and ran to the
door, leaving him alarmed, but he wasn’t

00:10:03.050 --> 00:10:07.730
quick enough to stop me, I unlocked it and
slipped out into the empty hallway.

00:10:07.730 --> 00:10:11.560
I didn’t really have much of a plan, other
than to hide.

00:10:11.560 --> 00:10:12.930
I looked left.

00:10:12.930 --> 00:10:19.589
Further down the hall, a girl was lying unconscious
on the floor with a guy in a black and white

00:10:19.589 --> 00:10:23.460
clown suit standing over her.

00:10:23.460 --> 00:10:25.700
He didn’t seem to have noticed me.

00:10:25.700 --> 00:10:27.050
I looked to the right.

00:10:27.050 --> 00:10:28.820
An empty hallway.

00:10:28.820 --> 00:10:30.430
Rows of lockers.

00:10:30.430 --> 00:10:32.010
And one trash can.

00:10:32.010 --> 00:10:36.580
I didn’t know if this would work, but I
didn’t really have another option.

00:10:36.580 --> 00:10:41.690
I quietly ran to my right, jumped, and landed
in the trash can, trying to make as little

00:10:41.690 --> 00:10:42.700
noise as possible.

00:10:42.700 --> 00:10:48.710
Lucky for me, the can was mostly empty, so
I was able to crouch down and not be seen

00:10:48.710 --> 00:10:50.140
poking out the top.

00:10:50.140 --> 00:10:54.140
It was quiet for a moment…

00:10:54.140 --> 00:10:59.030
Then… the clown horn started repeatedly
honking again…

00:10:59.030 --> 00:11:04.339
It was gradually getting louder, which meant
the clown was headed in my direction.

00:11:04.339 --> 00:11:10.190
My hiding spot was about to be tested.

00:11:16.520 --> 00:11:20.930
The clown yanked the rim of the garbage can,
and sending me tumbling out onto the floor!

00:11:20.930 --> 00:11:27.800
A pair of big, shiny, obsidian black eyes
was staring down as the clown stood over me

00:11:27.800 --> 00:11:30.360
with a disgusting grin.

00:11:30.360 --> 00:11:34.130
It was the face of an old style circus clown.

00:11:34.130 --> 00:11:39.010
He must have been wearing blackout contacts
or something and his face was completely greased

00:11:39.010 --> 00:11:44.070
down in white makeup, except for his lips
and the dots on his cheeks, both of which

00:11:44.070 --> 00:11:45.150
were painted black.

00:11:45.150 --> 00:11:50.090
In fact, his entire outfit was black and white,
making him look like he had stepped out of

00:11:50.090 --> 00:11:53.160
a black and white photograph and into reality.

00:11:53.160 --> 00:12:00.480
The only part that did look more cartoonish
was how very bloodthirsty his grin was.

00:12:00.480 --> 00:12:04.110
I was lying on my back on the floor where
I had been dumped out of the garbage can as

00:12:04.110 --> 00:12:06.510
this horrifying thing reached down for me.

00:12:06.510 --> 00:12:08.920
I only knew of one thing left to do.

00:12:08.920 --> 00:12:13.910
As hard as I could I kicked my foot up into
his balls!

00:12:13.910 --> 00:12:19.529
But to my shock and horror, this attack did
nothing to him!

00:12:19.529 --> 00:12:22.029
The clown didn’t even flinch.

00:12:22.029 --> 00:12:25.450
It seemed to cause him no pain whatsoever.

00:12:25.450 --> 00:12:29.620
I felt his silk gloves close around my neck
as he pinned me to the ground.

00:12:29.620 --> 00:12:35.100
I tried to scream, but I felt my throat close
up, and I knew it would do me no good anyway.

00:12:35.100 --> 00:12:42.730
All I could do was look up at this circus
drawn nightmare and… and there was something

00:12:42.730 --> 00:12:43.800
else…..

00:12:43.800 --> 00:12:47.450
Just above my head was someone’s overstuffed
locker.

00:12:47.450 --> 00:12:52.510
It wasn’t fully closed; the bottom of the
door was pushed open by some object that didn’t

00:12:52.510 --> 00:12:56.540
quite fit inside, but it looked like the owner
had tried to cram it shut anyhow.

00:12:56.540 --> 00:12:59.690
I reached for the locker door and yanked at
it.

00:12:59.690 --> 00:13:02.040
It gave a little bit, but it was stuck.

00:13:02.040 --> 00:13:03.720
I was starting to blackout.

00:13:03.720 --> 00:13:06.740
If I could just pull it free…

00:13:06.740 --> 00:13:10.170
I gave it a hard tug and pulled on it.

00:13:10.170 --> 00:13:15.510
My vision was fading, almost entirely black
now.

00:13:15.510 --> 00:13:21.260
I maybe only realized it had worked when I
heard the familiar sound of the locker flying

00:13:21.260 --> 00:13:27.100
open, and it crashed against the clown’s
head, knocking it backwards and off of me.

00:13:27.100 --> 00:13:30.399
An unbelievable amount of junk came pouring
out.

00:13:30.399 --> 00:13:34.290
Whatever was in there must have been heavy,
because it had really knocked the clown hard

00:13:34.290 --> 00:13:38.720
in the head, which was good because I also
needed a moment to come to.

00:13:38.720 --> 00:13:44.149
I had one more idea -- if this didn’t work,
I was done for.

00:13:44.149 --> 00:13:49.330
As fast as I could, I took all of the junk
out of the locker and hurled it at the clown.

00:13:49.330 --> 00:13:54.110
Textbooks, an instrument case, a pair of shoes;
anything I could find.

00:13:54.110 --> 00:13:58.490
The clown seemed woozy and it got back to
its feet and regained its bearings just as

00:13:58.490 --> 00:14:00.720
I threw my last piece of ammo.

00:14:00.720 --> 00:14:05.209
It seemed like none of the junk in that locker
was big enough to hurt the clown which didn’t

00:14:05.209 --> 00:14:09.220
seem to even feel or notice anything other
than the blow to it’s head.

00:14:09.220 --> 00:14:12.870
But hurting it wasn’t my plan.

00:14:12.870 --> 00:14:16.440
I had completely emptied out the locker.

00:14:16.440 --> 00:14:17.480
This was it.

00:14:17.480 --> 00:14:18.530
Do or die.

00:14:18.530 --> 00:14:23.910
I stepped back into the locker as the clown,
with a twisted face of anger and frustration,

00:14:23.910 --> 00:14:32.240
charged at me as I pulled the door shut as
much as possible without pinching my hand!

00:14:32.240 --> 00:14:37.020
Everything went black as I shut myself into
the locker and furious clown slammed into

00:14:37.020 --> 00:14:42.459
the door, effectively locking me in!

00:14:42.459 --> 00:14:51.790
There was no scream or roar of frustration,
just the echoey reverberation of the clown

00:14:51.790 --> 00:14:55.150
crashing up against the metal door.

00:14:55.150 --> 00:15:00.210
He fumbled with the handle shortly before
realizing that it was no good.

00:15:00.210 --> 00:15:04.120
Then I heard something move in the distance,
and the clown started beeping it’s horn

00:15:04.120 --> 00:15:07.960
once again, and heading off to some other
part of the school.

00:15:07.960 --> 00:15:16.510
I stayed safe in the that locker for hours
until the school was cleared and the principal

00:15:16.510 --> 00:15:18.720
used his master key to let me out.

00:15:18.720 --> 00:15:23.570
The light hurt my eyes as I collapsed onto
the hallway floor; I had been limited to the

00:15:23.570 --> 00:15:28.240
tiny amount of light that poured through three
thin slots on the locker door.

00:15:28.240 --> 00:15:32.820
The principal gave me a little nod, and told
me, “good thinking”, or something along

00:15:32.820 --> 00:15:37.140
those lines, before turning and attending
to the more important matters at hand.

00:15:37.140 --> 00:15:44.399
The hallway was now filled with police officers,
school administrators, news reporters, photographers…

00:15:44.399 --> 00:15:48.890
and… wait, what were Lexi’s parents doing
here?

00:15:48.890 --> 00:15:53.350
My best friend’s dad was standing maybe
15 feet down the hall with his arm around

00:15:53.350 --> 00:15:58.610
her mom, who was sobbing and dabbing at her
eyes as the commotion flowed around them like

00:15:58.610 --> 00:16:01.480
a rock cutting through a stream.

00:16:01.480 --> 00:16:03.960
What? What had happened?

00:16:03.970 --> 00:16:09.110
I looked around some more and realized they
weren’t the only ones.

00:16:09.110 --> 00:16:13.029
It looked like there were a few more sets
of parents in tears scattered around the hallway

00:16:13.029 --> 00:16:14.029
here and there.

00:16:14.029 --> 00:16:19.250
There were no other students around, I guess
the rest of the day’s classes had cancelled.

00:16:19.250 --> 00:16:23.000
Before I got up from off the floor where I
had fallen out of the locker, I noticed a

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:27.740
little ripped piece of fabric fall on the
ground right where I fell.

00:16:27.740 --> 00:16:31.730
It looked like it had been a piece of the
clown’s neck ruffle that had been caught

00:16:31.730 --> 00:16:36.460
in the closing locker door and probably ripped
off when it tried to escape.

00:16:36.460 --> 00:16:37.480
There was text on it.

00:16:37.480 --> 00:16:42.190
It said “...ipsey and Parks...”

00:16:42.190 --> 00:16:45.040
The rest was torn off and I couldn’t read
it.

00:16:45.040 --> 00:16:49.700
A bright flash filled the room.

00:16:49.700 --> 00:16:55.740
Reporters were taking pictures of Mr. Markham,
but to my surprise, he wasn’t being handcuffed

00:16:55.740 --> 00:16:58.050
or interrogated by angry parents.

00:16:58.050 --> 00:17:04.390
A news anchor wearing a tie and holding a
microphone started to praise him; going on about

00:17:04.390 --> 00:17:11.870
this one brave teacher whose heroics may have
saved the lives of countless students.

00:17:11.870 --> 00:17:16.110
Then he started going into this phony story
about how he immediately ran out to fight

00:17:16.110 --> 00:17:20.490
off the clown and protect the students the
moment the lockdown is called.

00:17:20.490 --> 00:17:25.170
Yeah, right, you’ve got to be kidding me!

00:17:25.170 --> 00:17:28.290
I was too drained to care though.

00:17:28.290 --> 00:17:34.000
I was crammed in a locker with no food and
not a big slot for air, and I really felt

00:17:34.000 --> 00:17:36.110
like I was going to black out again.

00:17:36.110 --> 00:17:41.100
I took a seat back down on the floor and closed
my eyes for a minute.

00:17:41.100 --> 00:17:45.400
Mr. Markham finished up his interview and
the reporter wrapped up the story.

00:17:45.400 --> 00:17:49.880
“This is the second clown attack our nation
has seen this week, after two students at

00:17:49.880 --> 00:17:54.480
a school in Garden Coast -- just yesterday
-- were fortunately unharmed during a lockdown

00:17:54.480 --> 00:17:55.480
incident.

00:17:55.480 --> 00:17:58.750
For CZN News 23, I’m Poppy Harlowe.”

00:17:58.750 --> 00:18:02.530
I looked around at the devastation surrounding
me.

00:18:02.530 --> 00:18:10.059
The incident was obviously over, but I still
felt this huge pit in my stomach, as if nothing

00:18:10.059 --> 00:18:11.480
had been resolved.

00:18:11.480 --> 00:18:15.910
Two clown attacks in one week?

00:18:15.910 --> 00:18:20.760
Sure the other school was probably nowhere
near here, but still.

00:18:20.760 --> 00:18:25.751
All the reporters and police officers seemed
to just be going about their business, as

00:18:25.751 --> 00:18:29.470
if this were just part of their routine or
something.

00:18:29.470 --> 00:18:30.720
Where was the urgency?

00:18:30.720 --> 00:18:34.400
Why wasn’t anyone doing anything about this?

00:18:34.400 --> 00:18:43.420
For a moment I got really angry, but then
the anger was just replaced with pain.

00:18:43.420 --> 00:18:47.220
My heart slowly broke as I sat there.

00:18:47.220 --> 00:18:51.450
I couldn’t get Lexi’s mom’s face out
of my head…

00:18:51.450 --> 00:18:54.830
Would I ever see Lexi again?

00:18:54.830 --> 00:18:57.660
Would school ever be the same?

00:18:57.660 --> 00:19:02.799
I’m pretty sure I knew the answer to both
questions when my parents arrived to pick

00:19:02.799 --> 00:19:04.450
me up.

00:19:04.450 --> 00:19:10.560
Both of their eyes were swollen and red...

